  "provenance": "Two profiles each execute four one-shot native Provider faults and four disabled-hook controls. Sixteen byte-identical product modules; new host-close module and refreshed root lock; provider runtime logic unchanged. All 16 processes exit live=0. Each injected case reports exactly one hook hit, three successful allocations and three frees; each control has two allocations/two frees. Test-only binaries link compiler-emitted product C to the native runtime from five Git objects at the pinned compiler revision. Raw provider metadata shortening and a post-write error exercise existing Provider rejection, temporary destruction and reservation rollback before explicit retry. Read-lease preflight, original token/table/data preservation, retained metadata charge, exact peaks, generation publication and final registry refund are asserted. No full-suite, Linux, packaging, isolation, DLL, performance or automatic Instance integration claim."
